WEBVTT

00:19.769 --> 00:24.274
Up until now, I thought I was the type
who gets along with everyone.

00:24.941 --> 00:25.942
Minato.

00:26.025 --> 00:27.360
But...

00:27.444 --> 00:28.695
Hey, Hikawa.

00:29.821 --> 00:33.199
My conversations
with her are always a little awkward.

00:33.283 --> 00:35.535
We just finished morning practice.

00:36.244 --> 00:38.246
Let's see, what is there to talk about?

00:38.788 --> 00:40.957
By the way, Igarashi was here yesterday.

00:41.041 --> 00:42.042
CRACK

00:42.125 --> 00:44.961
Sheesh, that face.
Did I just step on a land mine?

00:45.045 --> 00:46.421
WE HAD NO CONNECTION WHATSOEVER

00:46.504 --> 00:49.466
Right, they don't seem all that close
and Igarashi looked a bit intense.

00:49.549 --> 00:51.634
DIDN'T EXPECT THAT GORILLA TO GO
TO THIS SCHOOL - FOUL-MOUTHED?

00:51.718 --> 00:54.888
Maybe she didn't vibe with him...
I messed up.

00:55.472 --> 00:59.642
Or maybe middle school is
a topic I need to avoid entirely.

00:59.726 --> 01:00.894
I should've been more tactful.

01:02.062 --> 01:03.146
I'm sorry.

01:03.730 --> 01:06.483
Maybe we should give middle school a rest.

01:07.484 --> 01:09.027
No, that was awkward.

01:09.110 --> 01:11.946
This isn't going the way I'd hoped.

01:12.030 --> 01:13.490
We're getting nowhere.

01:13.990 --> 01:17.118
It's like the more I talk,
the deeper I sink...

01:17.869 --> 01:19.120
Huh?

01:19.204 --> 01:21.414
Was I always like this?

01:26.503 --> 01:27.504
WARM AND TOASTY

01:27.587 --> 01:29.255
That cool air feels nice.

01:30.840 --> 01:31.841
Koyun--

01:31.925 --> 01:34.511
Why must you stick your nose
into other people's business?

01:37.222 --> 01:38.681
I don't get it...

01:39.557 --> 01:41.476
I thought I could hear...

01:41.976 --> 01:43.019
You disgust me.

01:44.687 --> 01:46.397
...the key to her heart locking me out.

01:50.693 --> 01:53.113
Minato, what just...

01:53.196 --> 01:54.447
Wait, what happened?

01:54.531 --> 01:56.449
Yota, I think...

01:56.533 --> 01:59.202
Just don't go getting close
to Koyun for weird reasons.

02:00.328 --> 02:02.205
...Miki might kill me.

02:04.374 --> 02:05.375
What?

03:30.376 --> 03:35.924
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

03:36.507 --> 03:40.929
EPISODE 5
CHANGE

03:41.012 --> 03:43.431
NURSE'S OFFICE

03:43.514 --> 03:44.849
GLOOMY

03:44.933 --> 03:45.934
Good golly.

03:46.017 --> 03:47.435
KOYUKI IN THE NURSE'S OFFICE

03:47.518 --> 03:50.063
There you go, eating sweet bread
and calling it a meal...

03:50.146 --> 03:54.400
Noriko, is there a way to not get mad?

03:54.484 --> 03:57.654
- Wait, even someone like you gets mad?
- Hot... Chilly...

03:57.737 --> 03:59.030
I do.

03:59.113 --> 04:00.490
Did you get into a fight?

04:02.533 --> 04:06.454
Well, everyone gets upset sometimes.

04:06.537 --> 04:09.290
You don't have
to deal with things on your own.

04:10.875 --> 04:14.545
It'd be easier if I could lash out
and get it out of my system,

04:15.046 --> 04:17.715
but I'm not like that.

04:18.549 --> 04:20.802
I know that about myself, but...

04:21.844 --> 04:24.639
Actually, I end up regretting
saying something at all.

04:24.722 --> 04:25.723
I HATE MYSELF

04:25.807 --> 04:27.308
She's a handful.

04:27.809 --> 04:30.311
I don't know what happened,

04:30.395 --> 04:33.231
but it's important
to communicate how you feel.

04:33.314 --> 04:35.984
You have to use your words
if you don't like something.

04:36.067 --> 04:37.360
Communicate?

04:37.944 --> 04:38.945
No.

04:39.696 --> 04:43.241
At that moment, I lost my temper...

04:43.324 --> 04:44.575
You disgust me.

04:45.576 --> 04:47.078
...and I meant to hurt him.

04:48.079 --> 04:52.333
Not only that, I lashed out at him
without hearing him out first.

04:53.334 --> 04:55.253
The lingering frustration

04:55.336 --> 04:58.756
and regret for my own actions
keep spinning in my head.

05:00.842 --> 05:01.843
YUM-MELON

05:01.926 --> 05:02.927
All I want is peace.

05:03.011 --> 05:04.012
SIGH

05:04.095 --> 05:06.014
What're you saying?
You're still in your teens.

05:07.974 --> 05:09.183
There you are.

05:10.810 --> 05:14.022
Koyun! I'll eat here too.

05:14.105 --> 05:17.317
Good grief,
when'd my office turn into a café?

05:17.400 --> 05:18.693
Want some, Koyun?

05:18.776 --> 05:20.653
- No, thanks...
- Sheesh.

05:21.195 --> 05:22.780
What brings you here?

05:22.864 --> 05:26.534
Well, this morning,

05:26.617 --> 05:30.455
I overheard the conversation
between you guys by the entrance.

05:38.129 --> 05:39.589
I'M HERE
I NEED YOUR NAME AND CLASS

05:39.672 --> 05:41.591
Clean up your own mess
before you head out.

05:41.674 --> 05:42.800
- Will do.
- Okay.

05:42.884 --> 05:45.553
MAKING ROUNDS - PLEASE COME
TO THE TEACHER'S ROOM

05:46.179 --> 05:47.180
Say, Koyun.

05:47.722 --> 05:52.185
Minato doesn't understand personal space,
can be overbearing, has a big ego

05:52.268 --> 05:53.895
- and is surprisingly childish.
- Hey...

05:53.978 --> 05:56.147
He thinks the world revolves around him,

05:56.230 --> 05:58.149
but he's not a bad guy.

06:00.651 --> 06:02.945
Also, I need to come clean.

06:03.529 --> 06:06.824
Minato and I have known of you
since middle school.

06:07.575 --> 06:08.576
What?

06:09.160 --> 06:11.579
Though, we didn't know your name.

06:11.662 --> 06:15.500
It hit me when you mentioned
you were in the basketball club.

06:16.501 --> 06:18.961
Basketball club? How...

06:20.838 --> 06:25.176
Miki told us about how you were bullied.

06:28.679 --> 06:30.431
Morning, Koyun.

06:30.515 --> 06:33.768
For once, I got here with time to spare...

06:35.937 --> 06:39.107
What... the heck?

06:39.190 --> 06:40.316
Forget you saw anything.

06:40.399 --> 06:42.485
What do you mean, "Forget it"?

06:42.985 --> 06:44.278
Since when?

06:44.362 --> 06:46.781
Good question. The entire time?

06:49.158 --> 06:51.285
I can't wait for all this to end.

06:52.787 --> 06:55.581
Miki told you two...

06:55.665 --> 06:58.000
Please don't be angry with her.

06:58.084 --> 07:01.379
She was worried sick about you back then.

07:01.462 --> 07:02.964
Yeah, I understand.

07:03.047 --> 07:07.844
Miki told us that she didn't realize
her friend was struggling.

07:07.927 --> 07:10.763
That she couldn't help her friend at all.

07:11.264 --> 07:14.308
I keep thinking, "Why didn't she tell me?

07:14.809 --> 07:17.437
Am I that unreliable?"

07:18.229 --> 07:20.106
It makes me a little sad.

07:20.815 --> 07:23.151
It's not about you being unreliable.

07:23.234 --> 07:26.446
Maybe your friend
simply didn't want to worry you.

07:27.447 --> 07:29.365
You think so?

07:29.449 --> 07:30.450
SOB

07:30.533 --> 07:32.535
But I wish she was open with me!

07:32.618 --> 07:33.619
Miki!

07:34.245 --> 07:35.413
So...

07:35.496 --> 07:37.623
That's how it made her feel...

07:38.583 --> 07:40.626
I didn't confide in Miki because...

07:40.710 --> 07:42.420
Go, Miki!

07:43.713 --> 07:45.047
Nice!

07:45.131 --> 07:46.174
Gimme five!

07:46.257 --> 07:48.759
...Miki took club activities seriously

07:49.260 --> 07:52.054
while I only attended practice

07:52.138 --> 07:56.142
out of the fear of quitting.
It felt like we were polar opposites.

07:56.976 --> 08:01.981
It was never about trust
or her being unreliable.

08:04.442 --> 08:09.530
Minato must've pieced it together
when he saw the two of you.

08:09.614 --> 08:12.617
That you're the girl in the basketball
club Miki mentioned before.

08:13.117 --> 08:16.871
That must be why
Minato was concerned about you.

08:17.872 --> 08:18.915
So that's it.

08:20.458 --> 08:21.584
I'm sorry.

08:21.667 --> 08:23.920
Maybe we should give middle school a rest.

08:24.504 --> 08:26.923
That's why Amamiya said that...

08:27.924 --> 08:31.010
I completely misunderstood him, and I...

08:31.093 --> 08:32.428
PARANOID - SELF-CONSCIOUS

08:34.305 --> 08:35.306
How embarrassing!

08:35.389 --> 08:36.390
Koyun?

08:37.183 --> 08:40.061
No, I must give him a sincere apology.

08:40.561 --> 08:43.147
A sincere apology? That's a bit heavy.

08:43.231 --> 08:45.191
Want me to be the messenger?

08:45.274 --> 08:47.860
No. I must express my apologetic intent.

08:47.944 --> 08:49.195
Apologetic intent?

08:49.820 --> 08:52.698
I guess he isn't too bothered.

08:53.282 --> 08:55.701
Don't worry about it.
Besides, it's only Minato.

08:56.827 --> 08:58.412
Hey, Amamiya!

09:00.540 --> 09:02.416
Sorry. Over here.

09:04.293 --> 09:06.379
Hello?

09:07.672 --> 09:11.467
What? Are you mad, Amamiya?

09:12.051 --> 09:14.136
Sorry, I was spacing out.

09:14.220 --> 09:15.221
What?

09:15.304 --> 09:17.306
You surprised me.

09:17.390 --> 09:19.642
I thought you were upset
for a second there.

09:19.725 --> 09:23.563
Idiot. Minato's got a resting cranky face.

09:25.565 --> 09:28.484
Why must you stick your nose
into other people's business?

09:28.568 --> 09:33.531
Did she say that
because I was talking with Igarashi?

09:34.031 --> 09:36.742
But is it that big of a deal?

09:37.743 --> 09:41.831
They say, "Don't do unto others
what you wouldn't have them do unto you."

09:42.331 --> 09:44.500
But the opposite isn't necessarily okay?

09:45.293 --> 09:46.586
I don't understand.

09:47.086 --> 09:48.504
Or rather...

09:48.588 --> 09:50.881
we're too different.

09:50.965 --> 09:53.551
We've got completely different values
and outlooks on life.

09:54.343 --> 09:56.512
What's right to me...

09:57.847 --> 10:00.308
and what's right to her are too different.

10:01.100 --> 10:04.520
So no matter what I do for her,
it ends up upsetting her.

10:07.106 --> 10:11.277
So trying to help makes me sanctimonious?

10:11.360 --> 10:13.029
Is it, Miki?

10:14.488 --> 10:17.533
If we're talking about sanctimonious,
then she is too.

10:17.617 --> 10:21.787
She draws a clear line between the people
she likes and those she doesn't.

10:21.871 --> 10:24.457
She accepts Yota and Miki.

10:24.540 --> 10:27.043
Meanwhile, I'm a reject.

10:28.544 --> 10:29.545
MIFFED

10:29.629 --> 10:32.548
It's starting to make me upset.

10:32.632 --> 10:34.342
BOINK
WHOA - BAM

10:34.425 --> 10:35.926
What's the matter?

10:36.510 --> 10:39.430
All right.
I won't bother with her anymore.

10:39.513 --> 10:42.600
It doesn't benefit either of us,
and it's not worth worrying about.

10:42.683 --> 10:43.684
GRADE 1 CLASS 5

10:44.935 --> 10:45.936
Yota.

10:46.020 --> 10:48.731
Where were you during lunch?

10:50.524 --> 10:51.567
The bathroom?

10:51.651 --> 10:52.693
That long?

10:56.530 --> 11:00.451
The day's over, but I couldn't find
the right time to apologize.

11:01.035 --> 11:03.996
Wait, is there such a thing
as a good time to apologize?

11:04.080 --> 11:05.206
GOOD TIME TO APOLOGIZE

11:06.874 --> 11:09.251
I hope I can catch him tomorrow.

11:09.335 --> 11:10.711
See you, Minato.

11:10.795 --> 11:12.129
Bye.

11:31.023 --> 11:34.485
This whole time, not once,

11:34.568 --> 11:38.280
have I given him a fair chance.

11:39.323 --> 11:42.076
I made assumptions based on
what happened in the past

11:42.159 --> 11:44.745
and decided from the start
that we don't vibe.

11:45.496 --> 11:47.748
I rejected him
without ever getting to know him.

11:48.332 --> 11:52.503
I did something I'd hate to go through
to someone else without a thought.

11:58.843 --> 12:00.803
That expression...

12:00.886 --> 12:04.265
It's the face she makes
when her guard is up.

12:04.849 --> 12:08.060
I thought we'd be friends in time,

12:08.561 --> 12:11.021
but that was just my ego talking.

12:11.605 --> 12:12.857
I was arrogant.

12:13.357 --> 12:15.359
To her, I was just a nuisance.

12:15.985 --> 12:19.155
Maybe it was better
if I never bothered her to begin with.

12:19.238 --> 12:20.656
Amamiya!

12:21.240 --> 12:22.241
Huh?

12:24.702 --> 12:25.911
I'm sorry.

12:28.789 --> 12:32.418
Can we talk for a minute?

12:38.507 --> 12:40.885
Do you have time right now?

12:40.968 --> 12:43.971
Yeah. I've got time
to kill before my club starts.

12:46.140 --> 12:47.933
So...

12:48.517 --> 12:53.105
What do I even say? I'm ashamed.
I'm ashamed about everything.

12:53.189 --> 12:55.191
MISUNDERSTANDING
PARANOID - SELF-CONSCIOUS

12:56.650 --> 12:58.944
Sorry I was terrible to you.

12:59.445 --> 13:00.446
Okay.

13:00.529 --> 13:02.364
When you mentioned middle school,

13:02.448 --> 13:06.410
I was worried how you knew
what happened in middle school.

13:06.911 --> 13:11.790
Just thinking Igarashi told you
made my stomach churn.

13:12.625 --> 13:16.795
But Yota told me during lunch today
that it was all just a misunderstanding.

13:17.379 --> 13:18.380
Yota did?

13:21.926 --> 13:22.968
The bathroom?

13:23.052 --> 13:24.303
That guy...

13:25.095 --> 13:26.305
I...

13:26.889 --> 13:30.392
got ahead of myself,
and behaved poorly towards you.

13:30.893 --> 13:31.894
I...

13:32.937 --> 13:35.564
I... I...

13:35.648 --> 13:38.067
Words overflow in my mind,

13:38.567 --> 13:40.611
but I can't ever find
the right way to get them out.

13:40.694 --> 13:42.321
I WANT TO GIVE A PROPER APOLOGY
I WANT TO CHANGE

13:42.404 --> 13:43.822
FOR SELF-SATISFACTION?
FOR WHOSE SAKE?

13:43.906 --> 13:45.324
I WANT TO TELL HIM
TELL HIM WHAT?

13:45.407 --> 13:48.369
When words race through my mind,
when I try to get them out,

13:48.994 --> 13:51.455
they get mixed up in my throat.

13:51.539 --> 13:53.707
All these feelings I can't put into words

13:54.375 --> 13:56.418
try to escape by turning into tears.

13:57.461 --> 13:59.088
WHOA...!

13:59.171 --> 14:02.049
Don't cry, don't cry, don't cry!

14:02.132 --> 14:03.175
Why do I always...

14:03.259 --> 14:04.927
I owe him an apology. I can't cry.

14:05.010 --> 14:06.011
ONLY TEARING UP

14:06.095 --> 14:08.305
Hold it in, hold it in, hold it in!

14:08.389 --> 14:09.390
Hikawa.

14:10.015 --> 14:11.267
It's all right.

14:12.851 --> 14:15.187
You don't have to apologize profusely,

14:15.271 --> 14:17.398
and besides, I'm the one who troubled you.

14:17.481 --> 14:20.776
As if. I was upset until a moment ago.

14:20.859 --> 14:22.528
Why am I the one consoling her?

14:22.611 --> 14:24.905
You can let it out. What...

14:24.989 --> 14:26.907
TEARS FALLING

14:28.993 --> 14:31.537
When someone is kind
as I'm holding back tears,

14:32.288 --> 14:33.831
it all comes out at once...

14:34.498 --> 14:36.667
TEARS STREAMING DOWN

14:37.251 --> 14:38.294
She's crying.

14:39.879 --> 14:41.171
FRAYING - PILLING

14:41.255 --> 14:42.256
HIDE...

14:42.840 --> 14:44.174
I...

14:44.258 --> 14:45.759
IT ALL COMES FLOODING OUT
BAWLING

14:45.843 --> 14:48.429
I lied when I said
I don't have a connection with Igarashi.

14:48.512 --> 14:50.890
- What?
- Rather, it's the opposite.

14:51.640 --> 14:53.934
We don't get along anymore.

14:55.853 --> 14:57.980
Where are we carrying these to again?

14:58.063 --> 14:59.940
Turn left, then go straight.

15:02.026 --> 15:03.444
THEY'RE ALONE - CRYING

15:03.527 --> 15:04.695
BOUND TO BE MISUNDERSTOOD

15:05.779 --> 15:06.864
Hikawa.

15:09.283 --> 15:10.951
It's heavy.

15:11.660 --> 15:14.455
See this? What do you think?

15:14.955 --> 15:17.082
What're they doing?

15:17.166 --> 15:19.543
Maybe they found a rare monster.

15:20.544 --> 15:21.921
My parents are...

15:27.384 --> 15:28.719
Thank you.

15:31.388 --> 15:32.389
Who's this?

15:34.934 --> 15:36.310
It's my Pomeranian.

15:38.312 --> 15:39.730
She laughed.

15:42.066 --> 15:43.484
How cute.

15:48.155 --> 15:49.949
Well, I've gotta get going.

15:50.032 --> 15:51.158
Sorry.

15:51.241 --> 15:52.242
Bye.

15:55.371 --> 15:56.747
See you tomorrow.

15:57.373 --> 16:00.250
Okay. See you.

16:15.391 --> 16:18.018
Wait a minute.

16:18.602 --> 16:21.522
Hikawa said
she doesn't get along with Igarashi...

16:21.605 --> 16:23.399
But back then...

16:23.983 --> 16:26.276
Hey. Igarashi?

16:26.360 --> 16:28.028
Do you remember Hikawa?

16:32.157 --> 16:33.784
Hikawa?

16:33.867 --> 16:36.912
I don't remember anyone
by that name from middle school.

16:37.496 --> 16:38.497
Wait...

16:39.164 --> 16:40.624
What does it all mean?

16:41.125 --> 16:43.293
TODAY'S RECOMMENDATION
RAMEN FAIR

16:43.377 --> 16:45.295
RICE - BOWLS

16:45.379 --> 16:47.047
SPACING OUT

16:47.715 --> 16:50.134
It didn't look like
either of them was lying.

16:50.217 --> 16:51.760
Rather, it's the opposite.

16:51.844 --> 16:52.970
Who's that?

16:53.053 --> 16:55.055
What happened between them?

16:55.139 --> 16:57.474
Why must you stick your nose
into other people's business?

16:57.558 --> 16:58.559
SNAPPING OUT

16:59.309 --> 17:00.728
DEFLATED

17:01.854 --> 17:03.522
Is something wrong, Amamiya?

17:04.648 --> 17:05.691
It's nothing.

17:05.774 --> 17:06.775
GRR!

17:06.859 --> 17:09.945
Liar! You've been spacing out
this entire time.

17:10.029 --> 17:11.030
I'm listening.

17:11.113 --> 17:13.490
Then what was I talking about? Tell me!

17:13.574 --> 17:14.950
Aren't you a needy girlfriend.

17:15.034 --> 17:16.118
WHAT YOU JUST SAID

17:16.201 --> 17:19.496
Minato, your noodles will get soggy
if you keep spacing out.

17:19.997 --> 17:23.083
- What inspired that combination?
- They don't go together, do they?

17:23.167 --> 17:24.543
They're yummy.

17:24.626 --> 17:26.503
- Gluten galore.
- What?

17:26.587 --> 17:27.588
Yota.

17:27.671 --> 17:30.674
Yota told me during lunch today
that it was all just a misunderstanding.

17:31.633 --> 17:34.261
She calls him by his first name.

17:34.762 --> 17:37.765
With the exams out of the way,
we're heading into winter break.

17:38.265 --> 17:39.933
We'll have nothing in common...

17:45.272 --> 17:46.273
SLURP

17:46.356 --> 17:48.942
- So what?
- In one go? You're creeping me out!

17:51.278 --> 17:55.199
How will she react if I approach her
the next time we meet?

17:55.866 --> 17:59.870
Will she feel awkward?
Or will she keep a distance, like before?

17:59.953 --> 18:00.954
EPISODE ONE

18:02.748 --> 18:04.208
I'm out of ideas.

18:07.294 --> 18:08.712
BA-BUMP

18:09.338 --> 18:10.798
Amamiya.

18:10.881 --> 18:11.965
BLUSH

18:17.554 --> 18:18.722
What?

18:18.806 --> 18:21.058
Yesterday,

18:21.809 --> 18:24.728
I'm sorry I ended up crying
when I was trying to apologize.

18:24.812 --> 18:27.064
I must've been a mess.

18:27.898 --> 18:29.233
ABSENT-MINDED

18:29.316 --> 18:33.195
It's not that I thought
you'd forgive me if I cried.

18:33.987 --> 18:34.988
Don't worry.

18:35.572 --> 18:38.534
Well, sometimes, we get overwhelmed

18:38.617 --> 18:42.246
and end up crying
for no good reason, right?

18:42.329 --> 18:43.330
DUMBFOUNDED

18:43.413 --> 18:45.624
It happens to you too?

18:46.792 --> 18:48.127
- So what?
- What?

18:48.710 --> 18:51.380
You thought I wouldn't
be able to understand?

18:51.463 --> 18:54.633
- What?
- That's terrible.

18:54.716 --> 18:55.717
SOB SOB

18:55.801 --> 18:56.885
FLUSTER FLUSTER

18:56.969 --> 18:58.303
To be honest, I didn't expect it.

18:58.387 --> 18:59.388
AH

18:59.972 --> 19:04.226
I may not look it,
but I'm a sensitive guy.

19:06.353 --> 19:07.396
What's that face for?

19:12.359 --> 19:13.610
You're so rude.

19:19.074 --> 19:21.577
Well, I'm going this way.

19:21.660 --> 19:23.662
- For your club?
- You guessed it.

19:25.289 --> 19:26.415
Good luck.

19:27.666 --> 19:28.667
Okay.

19:43.473 --> 19:47.436
I shouldn't assume all the time
that people don't understand me

19:47.519 --> 19:50.105
or that they'll reject me.

19:53.275 --> 19:55.569
MIKI - COME TO MY WORK
OVER WINTER BREAK - SEE YA

19:55.652 --> 19:59.406
It's as if something changed
ever so slightly... or maybe not.

19:59.489 --> 20:00.699
I'LL INVITE YOTA TOO

20:01.992 --> 20:03.285
That's the vibe.

20:03.785 --> 20:07.372
Winter break starts tomorrow.

21:39.006 --> 21:41.174
KAWAII CAFE - WELCOME
WINTER BREAK FAIR

21:41.758 --> 21:45.929
Miharu! Sora! It's been a hot minute. Yay!

21:46.013 --> 21:47.222
Yay!

21:47.306 --> 21:48.432
How've you been?

21:48.515 --> 21:49.850
CATCHING UP WITH OLD FRIENDS

21:49.933 --> 21:52.686
Haven't seen you since we graduated.
How's high school going?

21:52.769 --> 21:54.521
It's peaceful and nice.

21:54.604 --> 21:57.524
Well? Are you two dating anyone?

21:57.607 --> 21:59.359
- Nope.
- Same.

21:59.443 --> 22:00.694
She didn't miss a beat.

22:00.777 --> 22:04.323
You went through boys in middle school.

22:04.406 --> 22:07.951
Like that handsome upperclassman and
the volleyball guy from another school.

22:08.910 --> 22:10.704
Well, that was...

22:10.787 --> 22:12.331
AN UPPERCLASSMAN
WITH NO CONNECTION WHATSOEVER

22:12.414 --> 22:14.041
He asked me out all of a sudden.

22:14.124 --> 22:15.125
MIGHT AS WELL!

22:15.208 --> 22:17.961
He grew on me, so I said yes.

22:18.045 --> 22:21.214
Every time I go out with a guy,
they call it off

22:21.298 --> 22:23.467
because I'm not who they thought I'd be.

22:24.551 --> 22:25.552
GRRR!

22:25.635 --> 22:29.181
Don't go creating an ideal version of me
and then get disappointed!

22:29.264 --> 22:31.391
She went full gorilla mode.

22:31.475 --> 22:32.976
Hey, sorry.

22:33.060 --> 22:36.980
All I'm saying is,
it doesn't count as going out.

22:37.064 --> 22:40.484
Next time I go steady with someone,

22:41.109 --> 22:46.073
I want to be the one to ask him out.

22:46.156 --> 22:47.783
Is there a guy you're into?

22:47.866 --> 22:48.867
Nobody.

22:49.826 --> 22:51.453
What about Amamiya?

22:51.536 --> 22:54.372
Bringing him up now
will only complicate things.

22:54.873 --> 22:56.249
What about you, Koyuki?

22:56.333 --> 22:58.001
Any boys in your life, Koyuki?

22:59.211 --> 23:00.295
Me?

23:04.257 --> 23:05.258
No, thanks.

23:06.551 --> 23:09.679
I don't think I'm cut out
for relationships.

23:10.347 --> 23:14.267
I admire the both of you
for keeping it going with your boyfriends.

23:15.936 --> 23:17.604
It's not that big of a deal.

23:18.605 --> 23:20.023
Do you have any pics?

23:20.107 --> 23:21.399
HEE HEE

23:21.483 --> 23:22.776
Can I show you?

23:24.402 --> 23:26.613
Gotta head off to work. See you.

23:26.696 --> 23:27.781
- See you!
- Bye bye.

23:27.864 --> 23:29.199
Let's hang out again.

23:31.368 --> 23:34.162
Koyuki's got it rough.

23:34.663 --> 23:38.291
What can she do?
There's what happened with Igarashi.

23:39.334 --> 23:43.255
To begin with,
why did she go out with Igarashi

23:43.338 --> 23:46.091
in middle school?

23:47.092 --> 23:48.927
I thought she hated his guts.

23:49.010 --> 23:51.221
Yeah, it surprised me too.

23:51.304 --> 23:53.849
I think I'm the one to blame.

23:53.932 --> 23:55.934
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
